exam: It is given that {p} pens are priced at {p*u} dollars in total. Determine the cost, in dollars, of {m} pens at the same price.
exam: Ascertain the sum in dollars payable for {m.words} notebooks, whereas {a} paid {p*u} dollars for {p.words} such notebooks.
exam: Whereas the cost of {p} identical items amounts to {p*u} dollars, state the cost of {m} such items, expressed in dollars.
exam: Compute the expenditure in dollars incurred by {b} in acquiring {m} cups, given that {p} cups of the same kind cost {p*u} dollars.
exercise: Grandad passed away and left {a} his old fountain pens. In the shop {p} of the same pens cost {p*u} dollars. How many dollars would {m} of them cost?
exercise: {a}'s mum was let go from the factory, so money's a bit tight. She paid {p*u} dollars for {p} school notebooks. How much would {m} notebooks cost at the same price?
test: shop calls it a "price adjustment", i call it robbery. {p} cans were {p*u} dollars. how much for {m} then, same price
